{"name":"Incense","hex":"#af9a7e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"incense","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Biotic material that releases fragrant smoke when burnt, often used in religious rites or for aesthetic reasons.","The fragrant smoke released by burning incense (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set on fire; to inflame; to kindle; to burn.","To anger; to infuriate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incense"}],"entries":[{"title":"Incense","blocks":[{"text":"Incense is an aromatic biotic material that releases fragrant smoke when burnt. The term is used for either the material or the aroma. Incense is used for aesthetic reasons, religious worship, aromatherapy, meditation, and ceremonial reasons. It may also be used as a simple deodorant or insect repellent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif/330px-R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incense","wikidata":"Q273131"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Incenselonghua.jpg/500px-Incenselonghua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Incenselonghua.jpg/500px-Incenselonghua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Burning incense at the Longhua Temple","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIncenselonghua.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg/500px-Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg/1280px-Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"